    <DataNode elementId="AT1G23310-MONOMER" textLabel="Glutamate--glyoxylate aminotransferase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LR30" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="435" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">AOAT1 (GGAT1) is peroxisomal located. Knock-out plants have reduced activity of AOAT, GPAT (glutamate:pyruvate aminotransferase), AGAT (alanine:glyoxylate aminotransferase) and GGAT (glutamate:glyoxylate aminotransferase). The GGAT and AGAT activities were reduced most drastically. These indicate AOAT1 is primarily involved in photorespiration|CITS:[12631323]|. Similary, AOAT2 (GGAT2), which is predicted to be located in the peroxisome, is likely involved in photorespiration. In vitro assay of the recombinant proteins indicated that GGAT1 and GGAT2 have four aminotransferase activities, namely GGAT, AGAT, GPAT and AOAT. The two recombinant proteins exhibited very similar Km values towards amino acid substrates glutamate and alanine, as well as the oxoacid substrates glyoxylate, pyruvate and 2-oxoglutarate|CITS: [12529529]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G23310-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G23310.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9LR30" />
